<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20309" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hĕbraei</span></b> , ōrum,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑβραῖοι</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the Hebrews</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hebraei, qui nunc Judaei: igitur et litterae
					Hebraeae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Apol. 18</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">postea vero cum in deserto consedissent,
					amiserunt vetus nomen Hebraei, et Judaei sunt appellati,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 4, 10</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 13, 8</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hĕbræus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to the Hebrews</i>, <i>Hebrew</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terrae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					5, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">liquores,</span>”
				i. e. <i>balsam</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 5, 1, 213</span></i>
			 (cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. 12, 25, 54, § 111</span></i>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lingua, litterae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug. Civ. D. 18, 39</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">42</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">codices,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 43</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hē^brā^ĭcus</span></b> ,
			a, 
			um, adj., the same: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plebes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Alcim. Avit. 5, 544</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scripturae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 4, 7</span></i>
			
			<i>fin.—Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hē^-brā^ĭcē</span></b> , <i>in the Hebrew language</i>, <i>in
				Hebrew</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hebraice Messias dicitur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 4, 7, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
